ext-decoration:underline;text-decoration:underline">reported</a><span>, Mac=
ron watched a new ballistic missile being fired from a French nuclear-power=
ed submarine, leaving it to his prime minister to try to reassure the Frenc=
h people that the government was on top of the crisis.</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>T=
hen things got worse.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,s=
erif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>By the time Macron finally spoke pub=
licly on Sunday, the student protests had snowballed into broader, violent =
riots across the country with many more people. Crowds smashed windows, bur=
ned cars, looted stores and vandalized public buildings, including the near=
-destruction of the historic town hall in the city of Limoges.</span></p><p=
 style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><=
span>Both the government=E2=80=99s failure to foresee the riots and its res=
ponse to them have been criticized across the political spectrum. Even befo=
re the violence, Macron=E2=80=99s approval rating stood at an abysmal 15 pe=
rcent. He doesn=E2=80=99t have much lower to fall.</span></p><p style=3D"fo=
nt:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>It=E2=
=80=99s all a far cry from 2017, when he took office at 39 years old, fresh=
-faced and confident, promising sweeping economic reforms to save France fr=
om stagnating growth, an ascendant far right and perhaps above all, a preva=
iling sense that France was no longer a functional society.</span></p><p st=
yle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><spa=
